(5843566, 848061, 59267, '<td valign="top">Very nice colorful lighting! This brought some imagination to me. Congratulations on 4th.</td>', 'Very nice colorful lighting! This brought some imagination to me. Congratulations on 4th.', '2010-01-29 15:13:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(5843834, 847943, 14476, '<td valign="top"><b>GREETINGS FROM THE CRITIQUE CLUB</b> <br/> <br/>Ohhh, when I saw this come up on my screen, I could hardly wait to see how it did in the scoring.  I loved it and gave it a 7. <br/> <br/>It is a beautiful image;  you handled it well.  Excellent lighting and good cropping on your model''s face.  It would (perhaps) have been better to have more of the face in the picture, and more or less of the clothing.  You "could" even here, have gone with a slightly closer crop to remove the blue...next time.  While I cannot get over the excellent lighting, the remainder of the composition has a great deal of merit as well, and keeping your helper relaxed and enjoying the shoot counts for a great deal.  It is fantastic experience should you decide on photography as a career.<br/> <br/>I look forward to seeing more of your work.<br/> <br/>Alice</td>', 'GREETINGS FROM THE CRITIQUE CLUB  Ohhh, when I saw this come up on my screen, I could hardly wait to see how it did in the scoring.  I loved it and gave it a 7.  It is a beautiful image;  you handled it well.  Excellent lighting and good cropping on your model''s face.  It would (perhaps) have been better to have more of the face in the picture, and more or less of the clothing.  You "could" even here, have gone with a slightly closer crop to remove the blue...next time.  While I cannot get over the excellent lighting, the remainder of the composition has a great deal of merit as well, and keeping your helper relaxed and enjoying the shoot counts for a great deal.  It is fantastic experience should you decide on photography as a career. I look forward to seeing more of your work. Alice', '2010-01-29 18:59:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(5843849, 847171, 14476, '<td valign="top"><b>GREETINGS FROM THE CRITIQUE CLUB</b> <br/> <br/>Well, it shows that you know your way around a camera.  The lighting and setup is delightful on this one, composition is just fine, exposure and placement in the frame works nicely.  <br/> <br/>So why did it end up at exactly at the 50% mark?  Could it be that since the theme was Bubbles, people expected to see bubbles front and center?<br/>Hmmm, maybe the name of the ''model'' is Bubbles;  who knows, could be.<br/>:-))<br/> <br/>I think you like to play around the edges of Challenge themes, and most of the time it works. This time?  Well...maybe, maybe not.  <br/> <br/>Oh, please continue to have fun with your well-planned and executed entries.<br/> <br/>I look forward to seeing more of them.<br/> <br/>Alice</td>', 'GREETINGS FROM THE CRITIQUE CLUB  Well, it shows that you know your way around a camera.  The lighting and setup is delightful on this one, composition is just fine, exposure and placement in the frame works nicely.   So why did it end up at exactly at the 50% mark?  Could it be that since the theme was Bubbles, people expected to see bubbles front and center?Hmmm, maybe the name of the ''model'' is Bubbles;  who knows, could be.:-)) I think you like to play around the edges of Challenge themes, and most of the time it works. This time?  Well...maybe, maybe not.   Oh, please continue to have fun with your well-planned and executed entries. I look forward to seeing more of them. Alice', '2010-01-29 19:18:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(5843914, 847995, 30982, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>First off, congrats on the top ten, an excellent score, and a new personal best!  I''d say this did very well!<br/> <br/>You definitely met the challenge, you received very high scores from your commenters, and the photograph is clean, crisp, and very well executed.  I really like the addition of the popped bubble - adds a bit of a different dimension from the simple bubble shot.  Your colors are rich without being oversaturated and the focus is crisp where it needs to be.  I''d love to offer ideas for improvement but I think you pretty much hit what you were after with this one!</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! First off, congrats on the top ten, an excellent score, and a new personal best!  I''d say this did very well! You definitely met the challenge, you received very high scores from your commenters, and the photograph is clean, crisp, and very well executed.  I really like the addition of the popped bubble - adds a bit of a different dimension from the simple bubble shot.  Your colors are rich without being oversaturated and the focus is crisp where it needs to be.  I''d love to offer ideas for improvement but I think you pretty much hit what you were after with this one!', '2010-01-29 20:57:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(5843923, 847771, 30982, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>A solid middle ground entry which suffered most likely from "did not meet challenge" votes - the number of "1" votes indicates that pretty strongly.  Since voters can''t see your comments during the challenge, they''d have no way of knowing immediately that the substance here is bubble mix.  That said, some seemed to think it was the psychedelic surface of a bubble, and the colors are rich and the focus is pretty good, with good even light.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! A solid middle ground entry which suffered most likely from "did not meet challenge" votes - the number of "1" votes indicates that pretty strongly.  Since voters can''t see your comments during the challenge, they''d have no way of knowing immediately that the substance here is bubble mix.  That said, some seemed to think it was the psychedelic surface of a bubble, and the colors are rich and the focus is pretty good, with good even light.', '2010-01-29 21:04:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(5843925, 847771, 30982, '<td valign="top">(oops - double post - sorry!)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-01-29 21:07:12.</i></td>', '(oops - double post - sorry!)', '2010-01-29 21:06:35.000000', '2010-01-29 21:07:12.000000', 0),
(5843929, 847459, 106543, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>This is my first critique, hopefully you find it helpful!<br/> <br/>First Impression: Very interesting image with many things happening. I didn''t notice the balloons on the box and was left wondering what exactly the bubbles were.<br/> <br/>Composition: I like the way the pole seems to split the image into two separate yet joined scenes.<br/> <br/>Subject: Good street photo with different things happening everywhere you look.<br/> <br/>Technical: As another commenter said there are not enough bubbles in this picture. If the bubbles at the top had not been cut off you would have received a higher score.<br/> <br/>Final thoughts: I was surprised to see you only scored a 5.02. I personally gave this shot a 7. I think this is due to the bubbles not being as much the main subject as other entries in this challenge.<br/> <br/>If you have any questions <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/messaging.php?action=compose&amp;USER_ID=106543" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">click here to message me</a>!<br/> <br/>Senay<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-01-29 21:14:17.</i></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! This is my first critique, hopefully you find it helpful! First Impression: Very interesting image with many things happening. I didn''t notice the balloons on the box and was left wondering what exactly the bubbles were. Composition: I like the way the pole seems to split the image into two separate yet joined scenes. Subject: Good street photo with different things happening everywhere you look. Technical: As another commenter said there are not enough bubbles in this picture. If the bubbles at the top had not been cut off you would have received a higher score. Final thoughts: I was surprised to see you only scored a 5.02. I personally gave this shot a 7. I think this is due to the bubbles not being as much the main subject as other entries in this challenge. If you have any questions click here to message me! Senay', '2010-01-29 21:12:30.000000', '2010-01-29 21:14:17.000000', 0),
(5844017, 846965, 113278, '<td valign="top">Great job on your first entry. You are even on the front page of the equipment photos for this camera. Keep it up.</td>', 'Great job on your first entry. You are even on the front page of the equipment photos for this camera. Keep it up.', '2010-01-29 22:29:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(5844027, 848145, 39850, '<td valign="top"><br/><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/35000-39999/39850/800/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_809051.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/35000-39999/39850/800/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_809051.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/35000-39999/39850/800/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_809051.jpg"/> <br/> <br/><u>Critique Club Critique</u> <br/> <br/><b>First Impressions</b> <br/>Nice colors, nice abstract.  Good fit for the Challenge, which I didn''t vote on.<br/> <br/><b>Photograph Information, Technicals &amp; Composition Review</b> <br/>I like the composition, but at first wondered whether it was upside down (or may benefit from a ''flip'').  My eye falls on the right places in the image where the focus is best.  The quality seems good and for an abstract style image, carries it over cleanly and well.<br/> <br/><b>Comments, Score &amp; Placement Review</b> <br/>A little surprised by placement of 32, however the subtlety of the ''bubbles'' maybe contributed to that.  Again, 5.70 is a little surprising, especially regarding the quality of the image itself.<br/> <br/>The comments seem to clearly articulate the appeal.<br/> <br/><b>Summary</b> <br/>Nice abstract that perhaps may have packed a little more punch with a bit of ''pp pop'' via tweaking of some colors and a little more depth/clarity added.  Perhaps even a slightly tighter crop on the right to emphasize, but still stands good as is.<br/> <br/>PS<br/>I see you''ve been at DPC for some time and this is your first Challenge entry - congratulations on taking the plunge and getting a decent score first up.</td>', '  Critique Club Critique  First Impressions Nice colors, nice abstract.  Good fit for the Challenge, which I didn''t vote on. Photograph Information, Technicals & Composition Review I like the composition, but at first wondered whether it was upside down (or may benefit from a ''flip'').  My eye falls on the right places in the image where the focus is best.  The quality seems good and for an abstract style image, carries it over cleanly and well. Comments, Score & Placement Review A little surprised by placement of 32, however the subtlety of the ''bubbles'' maybe contributed to that.  Again, 5.70 is a little surprising, especially regarding the quality of the image itself. The comments seem to clearly articulate the appeal. Summary Nice abstract that perhaps may have packed a little more punch with a bit of ''pp pop'' via tweaking of some colors and a little more depth/clarity added.  Perhaps even a slightly tighter crop on the right to emphasize, but still stands good as is. PSI see you''ve been at DPC for some time and this is your first Challenge entry - congratulations on taking the plunge and getting a decent score first up.', '2010-01-29 22:48:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(5844055, 847186, 18799, '<td valign="top">Hi, Critique Club here...<br/> <br/>This is a difficult image to critique because it is kind of an abstract and is so subjective by nature.<br/> <br/>But here goes.<br/> <br/>First what I like:<br/>I think the texture on the green side is very cool, almost reptilian with the varied shapes of the bubbles.  It''s sharp and the color really pops.  I rather like the transition to orange as well.  I like the linear line with reservations (see below)<br/> <br/>What I''m not so keen on:<br/>I find myself distracted by the out of focus bubbles along the bottom edge as well as the out of focus right side.  I find myself wishing the lower edge of the bubbles was more of a strait line, but once again, purely a taste thing.  I''m not particularly keen on all the darkness at the top and bottom and think the image should be cropped tighter - top, bottom, and from the right side.  As is, there really isn''t a place for my eye to focus, it''s kind of all over the place.  I might play with the diagonal idea that one commenter pointed out, that might make a more dynamic presentation.<br/> <br/>I hope this is somewhat helpful.<br/></td>', 'Hi, Critique Club here... This is a difficult image to critique because it is kind of an abstract and is so subjective by nature. But here goes. First what I like:I think the texture on the green side is very cool, almost reptilian with the varied shapes of the bubbles.  It''s sharp and the color really pops.  I rather like the transition to orange as well.  I like the linear line with reservations (see below) What I''m not so keen on:I find myself distracted by the out of focus bubbles along the bottom edge as well as the out of focus right side.  I find myself wishing the lower edge of the bubbles was more of a strait line, but once again, purely a taste thing.  I''m not particularly keen on all the darkness at the top and bottom and think the image should be cropped tighter - top, bottom, and from the right side.  As is, there really isn''t a place for my eye to focus, it''s kind of all over the place.  I might play with the diagonal idea that one commenter pointed out, that might make a more dynamic presentation. I hope this is somewhat helpful.', '2010-01-29 23:19:18.000000', NULL, 0),
